# M4.29.2 Monitor false success and SSH sandbox

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

After two complete stable Agentmode cycles, `tu1nz_monitor.service` had
`Result=success`, but external `monitor_last.txt` contained `🔴 Git Fehler`.

## Cause

The retained legacy monitor performs a read-only Docs `git ls-remote` through
the `chatops` SSH configuration. `ProtectHome=yes` hid that configuration from
the Monitor unit. Independently, the legacy script prints red check results but
can still exit zero; the external-state wrapper previously preserved only that
zero exit status.

## Impact

- no Control mutation or drift;
- Agentmode completed two full stable 300-second cycles;
- Integrity completed successfully with external evidence;
- Monitor evidence was contradictory and cannot be accepted as final;
- Adult Candidate remained inactive, dead, static and never started.

## Remediation and rollback

Use `ProtectHome=read-only` for Monitor so its existing deploy key remains
readable but no home directory is writable. Make the wrapper return non-zero
when captured output contains a red status marker, even if the legacy command
returns zero. Add regression tests, bind both new hashes, pass full CI, back up
the currently installed wrapper/unit, install only those two artifacts, and
rerun Monitor. On any red output or non-success result, restore the immediately
preceding bytes while the oneshot is inactive and leave Monitor stopped.
